<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xri version="1.0">
   <description>
      <p>AutoPano - one-button seamless mosaic of linear deep-sky panels (plate solving, star refinement, photometry, seams, noise matching, seam editing).</p>
   </description>
   <platform os="all" arch="noarch" version="1.9.5:1.9.99">
      <package fileName="AutoPano-1.0.2-20261015.zip" sha1="d15190146f664e2e3f28679aadc6d97221c21eb0" type="script" releaseDate="20261015">
         <title>AutoPano 1.0.2</title>
         <description>
            <p>Mosaics of large galaxies and nebulae: backgrounds are matched over the whole overlaps (not only empty sky), so no steps when an object fills the panels; GraXpert option in two steps (panels with enough empty sky, then the whole seamless mosaic) - removes light-pollution domes without cutting a large object's halo; fixed noise estimate on object-filled panels (no NaN, no blotchy added grain); FITS / any file names; the Astrometry column shows panels solved during the build.</p>
            <p>After installation the script is available as Script &gt; Utilities &gt; AutoPano.</p>
         </description>
      </package>
   </platform>
</xri>
